!Proposed definitions

;__da__ (KOhA1): something 1. Logically quantifiable singular variable. 
ro da poi gapkla cu nitkla
''Everything that goes up, comes down.''
;__de__ (KOhA1): something 2. Logically quantifiable singular variable.
su'o da su'o de gapkla gi'e stali
''Something goes up somewhere and stays there.''
;__di__ (KOhA1): something 3. Logically quantifiable singular variable.
pa da broda ijo ge su'o de broda gi ro di poi broda cu du de
''Exactly one thing1 is a broda iff some thing2 is a broda and every thing3 that is a broda is that thing2.''  

!!Notes

* da, de, di are __singular__ variables because they take values one at a time. The quantifier indicates the number of values it can take such that with each of those values the relationship is true. A __plural__ variable could take more than one value at once to satisfy a predicate.
 